    "rich_text_p7D8ce": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "spacer_L8mYri": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "heading_MrGjAB": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "FAQ",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "heading_font_class": "fs-heading-3-base"
          }
        },
        "border_JMAjFR": {
          "type": "border",
          "settings": {}
        },
        "subheading_jRWLhL": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How do I choose between 2\", 2.25\", 2.75\", and 3\" white pillar candles?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_cVFhCr": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose 2\" and 2.25\" pillars when you want a cleaner, lighter arrangement that leaves more room for florals, greenery, or table décor. Choose 2.75\" and 3\" pillars when the candles need to look fuller and take on more of the visual weight in the setup.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_ykeVbb": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_fVaWkq": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which white pillar sizes are easiest to repeat across several tables?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_xVMDY7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The 2\" x 3\", 2\" x 4\", and 2\" x 6\" packs are the easiest sizes to repeat across several tables because they come in 20-packs and are simple to work into classic event or dining layouts. They give you a clean white pillar look without moving into the bulkier widths too quickly.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_68L9WH": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_63Jihh": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which white pillars work best when I want a fuller centerpiece?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_dttHE3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The 2.75\" x 5\", 2.75\" x 6.6\", and 3\" pillar formats are usually the better choice for fuller centerpieces. Those sizes have more body, so they stand up better next to larger florals, wider trays, and more substantial decorative pieces.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_7QXgMW": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_TCpCmP": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What is the easiest way to create a layered all-white pillar arrangement?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_zpDMyy": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Start with one of the grouped sets instead of building the mix one candle at a time. The round set of 18 with 3\" x 4\", 3\" x 6\", and 3\" x 9\" pillars is a practical option when you want varied height inside one white pillar candle plan.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_T6Cpcf": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_C6d8PF": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "When do white pillar candles work better than ivory pillar candles?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_Nq7qRa": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>White pillars work better when you want a cleaner, brighter contrast in the room. They are especially useful with crisp white linens, clear glass, cooler palettes, formal ceremony styling, and minimalist interiors, where a soft ivory tone would blend in more seamlessly.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_dTL4pf": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_8nYt8z": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Are white pillar candles a good choice for weddings?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_VH7yLh": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, white pillar candles are an excellent and easy choice for weddings when the décor calls for a bright, classic candle color. At Kisco Candles, shoppers usually choose them for centerpieces, ceremony clusters, and formal event styling, where a crisp white look is cleaner and more defined than ivory.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_dpe9RU": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_MehrQH": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Can I mix several white pillar sizes in one order and still keep the look cohesive?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_zhjM6a": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, you can mix sizes and keep the look cohesive as long as you stay inside one white pillar assortment. At Kisco Candles, we offer you several widths, heights, and grouped formats of white pillar candles, making it easier to create variation without breaking the clean white color story.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_fmx8zR": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_zG33aG": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which white pillar products make the most sense for venues, planners, or regular restocking?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_wGfWWF": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The larger repeatable packs, especially the 20-packs in the 2\" line, make the most sense when you need the same candle look across many tables or recurring setups. They are more practical for venue and planner use than buying a stack of small mixed boxes each time.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_V9cHAP": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_kNtkHN": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which white pillar candles are easiest to use across several tables?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_qwDxnJ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The 2\" white pillar sizes are usually the easiest to repeat across several tables. They create a clean, consistent look, fit more comfortably into centerpieces, and are easier to group in pairs or sets without making the table feel too full.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_fFjiCx": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_b9QkyQ": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which white pillar candle sizes do you offer?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_7PjjhC": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>At Kisco Candles, you can order white pillar candles in several widths and heights, including slimmer 2\" styles, wider 2.25\", 2.75\", and 3\" options, plus mixed-height sets for more layered arrangements. That makes it easier to choose a simple, single-size look or build a fuller white centerpiece with more dimension.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        }
      },
